</figure>

<div class="legende-triplex">
    <span><span class="pastille laon"></span>Laon, above (the rhythm)</span>
    <span><span class="pastille vat"></span>Square notation, centre (the notes)</span>
    <span><span class="pastille sg"></span>St. Gall, below (the gesture)</span>
</div>

<div class="encadre">
    <span class="etiquette">Key point for this chant</span>
    <p>
        <span class="mot-latin">Victimæ paschali laudes</span> illustrates the
        <strong>syllabic</strong> style and the <strong>strophic</strong> form of the
        sequence. After the abundance of the graduals, it is a return to clarity&nbsp;: one
        note, one syllable, one word — and the Easter text offering itself almost as a
        narrative.
    </p>
</div>

